  "body": "Signed-off-by: Zach Aller <zach_aller@intuit.com>\n",
  "references": [
    {
      "commit": {
        "author": "\"Zach Aller\" <code@example.com>",
        "date": "2026-10-28T16:29:41-06:00",
        "subject": "ci: post the Codecov comment only after every coverage upload has arrived (#2357)",
        "body": "* ci: post the Codecov comment only after every coverage upload has arrived\n\nA pull request commit receives five coverage uploads: integration and ui from\nci.yaml and one e2e upload per Kubernetes version from ci-e2e.yaml. The e2e\nworkflow usually finishes first, and Codecov posted the PR comment on the\nfirst upload and never refreshed it, so the comment compared e2e-only\ncoverage (about 49%) against a complete base (about 85%); #2348 and #2356\nboth showed that. The status checks use the merged report and were never\naffected. Wait for all uploads before commenting.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BmNNrkL768qXPQxYGu5Tz2\nSigned-off-by: Michael Crenshaw <350466+crenshaw-dev@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* ci: Codecov counts the e2e matrix as one report, so wait for three\n\nWith after_n_builds: 5 no comment was posted on this PR although all\nuploads arrived; the three e2e matrix uploads share one name and flag and\ncount once.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BmNNrkL768qXPQxYGu5Tz2\nSigned-off-by: Michael Crenshaw <350466+crenshaw-dev@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Michael Crenshaw <350466+crenshaw-dev@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
        "sha": "8892b48e15c6c5964e10d08d9bb5c4f283fae1a0",
        "repoUrl": "https://github.com/argoproj-labs/gitops-promoter"
      }
    }
  ]
}
